## 4. Stream the Logs to Termux
To keep your setup mobile, use Termux to log into your Ubuntu server via SSH. You can watch the raw traffic hit your server in real-time from your phone:

ssh user@YOUR_UBUNTU_IP# Once inside, watch incoming raw connections using tcpdump:
sudo tcpdump -i any port 53 or port 80 or port 389 -vv

By cutting out Cloudflare entirely and using your Ubuntu server's direct IP, you unlock an unthrottled environment capable of catching every single type of OOB interaction.
